<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#" xmlns:swrl="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#" xmlns:swrlb="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrlb#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:base="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/">
  <!--
						This namespace contains classes and properties of the Globalise Ontology. The Globalise Ontology is an extension of the CIDOC CRM ontology family that has been devised bottom up during the course of the Globalise project. The Globalise project deals with the representation of historical data identified and documented in the research of the Dutch East Indies company archival dataset. This ontology is project specific and intended to represent data structures that go beyond the standard modelling of the reference ontology of the project and represent important entities and relations between entities for the project documentation scope. It supplements the high level ontologies that it borrows from in order to support the semantic modelling required to represent the information space of this project.  Compatibility and Nomenclature    CIDOC CRM v.7.1.3  AAAo v.2.0  PWRo v.0.9    The specification consists of a set of declarations for formalized classes and properties that extend the CIDOC CRM and the above official extensions.   Adopting the conventions of the CIDOC CRM each class and property have been given an identifier in addition to their names. The naming convention adopted for this extension is:  G = classGR = property  The choice of these names was arbitrary, making a conceptual connection with the official CRM representation while clearly distinguishing the new classes and properties from those of either CRM base or its official extensions.  Namespace: https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/   Ontology Development  We adopt the OntoMe tool developed by LARHRA to manage the ontology and produce editions. This ensures a consistent management of the ontology and provides a public space to engage in revisions.  The maintenance space for the ontology can be found here: https://ontome.net/project/202  Acknowledgements  The development of the Globalise Ontology has been made possible in part via contributions from:     Takin.solutions  Globalise Project  
						Exported from OntoME: Globalise Ontology ongoing
						Official URI : https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/
						-->
 <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G1_Financial_Exchange">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G1</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Financial exchange is an intentional act, undertaken by two or more actors, to determine the value of one set of goods, commodities or currencies, in exchange for another set of goods, commodities or currencies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Financial Exchange</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE13_Speech_Act"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE13_Speech_Act"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G2_Exchange_Value">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G2</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An instance of exchange value is the collective ascription of a form of equivalence between two currencies or commodities decided through the context of a G1 Financial Exchange. The substance of the exchange value is the communal commitment to the equivalence of the two currencies or commodities in question.
Instances of exchange value come to be through the process of negotiation and trade, though they may have arisen through habit, fiat or be of unknown origin. Instances of exchange value end either through a formal process, such as a new negotiation or trade, the formal fixing of an alternate exchange value for a given currency or commodity (which may also be null in the case of defunct government or authority), be eliminated by fiat or be of unknown reason.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Exchange Value</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE1_Institutional_Fact"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE1_Institutional_Fact"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G3_Commodity">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G3</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This class comprises types that stand in for instances of E19 Physical Object, the outcome of a production process that as produced some good (such as silk or lumber), but which are not intended to be used (or documented) as individual entities. Their function is to act as a sort of measure for sales or the exchange of other goods. Acting as form of currency, their existence qua 'type' is principally confined to account books and ledgers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Commodity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G4_Exchange_Unit">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G4</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This class comprises the unit types that may apply to the kinds of things exchanged in a financial exchange, including currencies, but also units typically employed in the exchange of commodities (e.g., bottles, barrels, crates, bales or cords).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Exchange Unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E58_Measurement_Unit"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G5_Payment">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G5</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This class comprises the intentional act of transferring an amount of currency or commodity from one actor to another.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Payment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E7_Activity"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G6_Purchase">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G6</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This class comprises the intentional act of transferring some amount of currency or commodity in exchange for some concrete (non-commodified) physical object, after which the physical object changes ownership from the actor who made the payment to the actor who received the payment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Purchase</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G5_Payment"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE20_Declarative_Acquisition"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE20_Declarative_Acquisition"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G7_Internal_State">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G7</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The temporal state in which someone or something (which may be intangible) is in.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Internal State</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E2_Temporal_Entity"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G8_Internal_Change">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G8</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An event class where the internal state of someone or something has changed in some manner.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Internal Change</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E5_Event"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G9_Attestation">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G9</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This class comprises events wherein there is written or spoken account of an entity or a state of affairs that is taken by the attester to be true. If these accounts are written, traces of them will be retrievable in the form of documentary evidence drawn from archival sources.
Instances of this class come into existence when an actor makes a propositional claim about something they belief to be true. Instances of this class cease to be when all documentary evidence of the attestation has disappeared and/or its existence has faded from memory.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Attestation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E13_Attribute_Assignment"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdfs:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G10_Successor_Status">
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">G10</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An instance of succession status is a collective ascription to a sovereignty of a successive association to another sovereignty. As opposed to a sovereignty following another one merely temporally, as in the case where a sovereign line is broken, the succession relation created between sovereignties is created by the socially recognized connection holding between them. In such cases, the sequence of sovereignties are taken to represent a unified lineage, the exact ordering of which may be the subject of research or scholarly debate, but we do have de jure attribution from which some knowledge may be derived and documented with an instance of Succession Status.
Instances of succession status are recognizable through evidence of community members adopting the intentional stance of so-recognizing this status, as observable from direct witnesses, through the reports of competent observers or through evidence of a declarative act initiating this status. Instances of locative status may come to be through a formal process such as a declaration of succession on the part of some sovereign, or may have arisen through habit, fiat or be of unknown origin. Instances of succession status may end either though a formal process, such as a new declarative act, or may simply fade out of use, be eliminated by fiat or be of unknown reason.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Successor Status</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE1_Institutional_Fact"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZE1_Institutional_Fact"/>
  </rdfs:Class>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR1_has_exchange_value_subject">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link the exchange value determined in a financial exchange to an amount to be exchanged.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has exchange value subject</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR1</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G2_Exchange_Value"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP1_has_intentional_subject"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR2_ascribes_exchange_value_equivalent">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link the exchange value determined in a financial exchange to an amount that has been exchanged for another amount.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ascribes exchange value equivalent</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR2</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G2_Exchange_Value"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP2_ascribes_intentional_target"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR3_ascribes_exchange_value_relation">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the specific type of exchange value which is indicated as holding between the subject amount and the target amount to be exchanged.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ascribes exchange value relation</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR3</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G2_Exchange_Value"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP3_ascribes_intentional_relation"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR4_is_dimension_of_commodity_type">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G3_Commodity"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link a commodity to a dimension that records its numeric amount.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is dimension of commodity type</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR4</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR5_paid_amount_to">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E39_Actor"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link a payment to an actor receiving that payment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">paid amount to</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR5</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G5_Payment"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR6_paid_amount">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link a payment to an amount paid in the payment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">paid amount</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR6</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G5_Payment"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR7_changed_internal_state">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G7_Internal_State"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is to link an internal change to an internal state that has been changed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">changed internal state</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR7</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G8_Internal_Change"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR8_is_internal_state_of">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is to link an internal state to a physical thing whose internal state it is.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is internal state of</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR8</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G7_Internal_State"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR9_attested_to">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E1_CRM_Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link an attestation to an entity attested to in the attestation</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">attested to</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR9</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G9_Attestation"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR10_has_successor_status_subject">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="WE2_Sovereignty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the sovereignty for which an succession status holds as institutional fact.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has successor status subject</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR10</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G10_Successor_Status"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP1_has_intentional_subject"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR11_ascribes_succeeded_sovereignty">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="WE2_Sovereignty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the sovereignty which has been succeeded by its successor.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ascribes succeeded sovereignty</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR11</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G10_Successor_Status"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP2_ascribes_intentional_target"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR12_ascribes_succession_relation">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the specific manner in which the succession which is indicated as holding for the sovereignty subject of the successor status pertains to this subject.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ascribes succession relation</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR12</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G10_Successor_Status"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP3_ascribes_intentional_relation"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR13_is_witnessed_by">
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E89_Propositional_Object"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link an attestation to a propositional object that records the trace of that attestation in verbal and/or visual form, as in e.g. a letter or brief.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is witnessed by</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR13</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G9_Attestation"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR1i_is_exchange_value_subject_of">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link the exchange value determined in a financial exchange to an amount to be exchanged.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is exchange value subject of</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR1i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G2_Exchange_Value"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP1i_is_intentional_subject_of"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR2i_is_exchange_value_equivalent_ascribed_by">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link the exchange value determined in a financial exchange to an amount that has been exchanged for another amount.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is exchange value equivalent ascribed by</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR2i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G2_Exchange_Value"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP2i_is_intentional_target_ascribed_by"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR3i_is_exchange_value_relation_ascribed_by">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the specific type of exchange value which is indicated as holding between the subject amount and the target amount to be exchanged.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is exchange value relation ascribed by</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR3i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G2_Exchange_Value"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP3i_is_intentional_relation_ascribed_by"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR4i_has_commodity_type_dimension">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G3_Commodity"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link a commodity to a dimension that records its numeric amount.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has commodity type dimension</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR4i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR5i_received_amount_from">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E39_Actor"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link a payment to an actor receiving that payment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">received amount from</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR5i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G5_Payment"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR6i_was_amount_paid">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E54_Dimension"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link a payment to an amount paid in the payment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">was amount paid</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR6i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G5_Payment"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR7i_was_internal_state_changed_by">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G7_Internal_State"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is to link an internal change to an internal state that has been changed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">was internal state changed by</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR7i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G8_Internal_Change"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR8i_has_internal_state">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E18_Physical_Thing"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is to link an internal state to a physical thing whose internal state it is.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has internal state</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR8i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G7_Internal_State"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR9i_was_attested_to_by">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E1_CRM_Entity"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link an attestation to an entity attested to in the attestation</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">was attested to by</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR9i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G9_Attestation"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR10i_is_successor_status_subject_of">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="WE2_Sovereignty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the sovereignty for which an succession status holds as institutional fact.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is successor status subject of</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR10i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G10_Successor_Status"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP1i_is_intentional_subject_of"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR11i_is_succeeded_sovereignty_ascribed_by">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="WE2_Sovereignty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the sovereignty which has been succeeded by its successor.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is succeeded sovereignty ascribed by</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR11i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G10_Successor_Status"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP2i_is_intentional_target_ascribed_by"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR12i_is_succession_relation_ascribed_by">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to indicate the specific manner in which the succession which is indicated as holding for the sovereignty subject of the successor status pertains to this subject.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is succession relation ascribed by</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR12i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G10_Successor_Status"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.swissartresearch.net/aaao/ZP3i_is_intentional_relation_ascribed_by"/>
  </rdf:Property>
  <rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/GR13i_witnesses">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E89_Propositional_Object"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property is used to link an attestation to a propositional object that records the trace of that attestation in verbal and/or visual form, as in e.g. a letter or brief.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">witnesses</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GR13i</skos:notation>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/globalise/ontology/G9_Attestation"/>
  </rdf:Property>
</rdf:RDF>
